-- title:
--   The terminal sequence of resolvents
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $K$ be closed and convex, $T$ nonexpansive with resolvents $R_n$, and $x\in K$.
--
--   1. **Terminal sequence.**
--   $$
--   b_j=R_{j+1}(x)\qquad(j=0,1,2,\dots),
--   $$
--   with defect $\|Tb_j-b_j\|\le1/(j+1)$ when $\operatorname{diam}K\le1$. For every fixed finite family of generated maps $g$, the total displacement $\sum_g\|g(b_j)-b_j\|$ tends to $0$ along this one sequence. The common terminal point of the switching argument is a limit along it.
